exists su name hymn verse one prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing Verse 1 of a lyrical song based on source text.

Rules:
- 3 to 5 short lines.
- 22 to 70 words total.
- Ground imagery and facts in the provided source text.
- Emotional, singable language.
- Plain text only.
- No labels, no bullets, no markdown, no surrounding quotes..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name hymn chorus prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing the Chorus of a lyrical song.

Rules:
- 2 to 4 short lines.
- 10 to 42 words total.
- Memorable and repeatable refrain.
- Keep the core theme tied to the source and Verse 1.
- Plain text only.
- No labels, no bullets, no markdown, no surrounding quotes..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name hymn verse two prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing Verse 2 of the same lyrical song.

Rules:
- 3 to 5 short lines.
- 22 to 70 words total.
- Focus on a different supported aspect than Verse 1.
- Do not repeat Verse 1 wording.
- Plain text only.
- No labels, no bullets, no markdown, no surrounding quotes..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name hymn bridge prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing the Bridge of the same lyrical song.

Rules:
- 2 to 4 short lines.
- 12 to 50 words total.
- Create an emotional turn or resolution.
- Keep continuity with prior sections.
- Plain text only.
- No labels, no bullets, no markdown, no surrounding quotes..text.quoted be text ya

